@jhaarblockware @mmjukic Because profit margins & cash flows would collapse; followed by equity prices and bond prices; which would take down everything else.

Pretend you & I both have factories: You pay 20% of costs for energy, I pay 0%.

How long until you go out of biz?

@pulte People buy houses as hard asset investments if they have poor alternatives.

If gold and BTC are allowed to rise to reflect USD debasement, the attractiveness of single-family homes as debasement hedges declines.

Higher gold & BTC is very socially useful in that way.

@jhaarblockware @mmjukic In a narrow vacuum, yes.

In a "free energy" scenario, all financial assets would collapse, & as a result, all assets with a financial tie would collapse alongside them.

IE BTC & gold would do what they did in COVID, except probably fall closer to $0 (before exploding higher).
